#
# Where rustup keeps the Rust mise.toml installs, and cargo its registry
# and binaries, on Windows: inside mise's own data folder, which
# FLEDGE_RUST_HOMES names. rustup and cargo ask Windows for the
# account's profile folder and ignore HOME, so without this every
# workspace of the account would share one store in it, and a rustup the
# person installed themselves would share it too. mise reads the two
# variables from [env], ahead of its rust.rustup_home and
# rust.cargo_home settings, for itself and for what it runs. mise.toml
# loads this file on Windows only.
RUSTUP_HOME=${FLEDGE_RUST_HOMES}/rustup
CARGO_HOME=${FLEDGE_RUST_HOMES}/cargo
